@format 1
@id section-naming.unnamed-section-display
@title Display an unnamed section
@section Section naming
@area In Split tab
@entry section-row-render,viewfinder-render
@summary Distinguish the localized Sections-panel placeholder for an empty stored main name from the real LPieceName, and show how affixes and Viewfinder labels behave while the section remains unnamed.
@related section-naming.inline-editor-open, section-naming.common.apply-name-state
@tag section
@tag split
@tag naming
@tag unnamed
@tag display

@alias panel = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSection
@alias viewfinder = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PViewfinder

[section-row-render] Sections-panel row rendering <input>
~ This starts with sections-panel row rendering.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionTextBuild checks whether LPieceName is empty when rendering a non-editing row @ panel.PSectionTextBuild(...)
> panel-name-check

[viewfinder-render] Viewfinder section rendering <input>
~ This starts with viewfinder section rendering.
[Technical explanation]
- PViewfinderSectionDraw receives the actual stored LPieceName for each section @ viewfinder.PViewfinderSectionDraw(...)
> viewfinder-name-check

[panel-name-check] Stored main name empty <decision>
~ The program checks stored main name empty.
[Technical explanation]
- An empty LPieceName uses PSectionPlaceholderFormat; a nonempty LPieceName is shown directly @ panel.PSectionTextBuild(...)
@ panel.PSectionPlaceholderFormat(...)
? "LPieceName empty" > placeholder
? "LPieceName nonempty" > stored-name

[placeholder] Show localized default-name placeholder <process>
~ This step handles show localized default-name placeholder.
[Technical explanation]
- Render Section.DefaultName for the row index using the muted brush; this placeholder is presentation only and is not written into LPieceName @ panel.PSectionPlaceholderFormat(...)
> panel-name-join

[stored-name] Show actual stored main name <process>
~ This step handles show actual stored main name.
[Technical explanation]
- Render LPieceName as the row's primary name text @ panel.PSectionTextBuild(...)
> panel-name-join

[panel-name-join] Panel main-name paths converge <junction>
> affixes

[affixes] Append stored affixes when present <output>
~ This path ends with append stored affixes when present.
[Technical explanation]
- PSectionAffixAdd appends each nonempty prefix and suffix after the primary display text, so affixes can therefore be visible even when the main name itself is empty @ panel.PSectionAffixAdd(...)

[viewfinder-name-check] Viewfinder can show main name <decision>
~ The program checks viewfinder can show main name.
[Technical explanation]
- PViewfinderSectionDraw renders a name only when LPieceName is nonempty and sufficient horizontal room remains after the numbered badge @ viewfinder.PViewfinderSectionDraw(...)
? "Empty name or insufficient room" > no-viewfinder-name
? "Nonempty name with room" > show-viewfinder-name

[no-viewfinder-name] Viewfinder shows no placeholder name <output>
~ This path ends with viewfinder shows no placeholder name.
[Technical explanation]
= The numbered section badge remains, but the localized Sections-panel placeholder is not substituted as a Viewfinder name.

[show-viewfinder-name] Show actual main name <output>
~ This path ends with show actual main name.
[Technical explanation]
= The Viewfinder shows LPieceName only; prefix and suffix are not included in this label.
